  "explanation": "<strong>Step 1: Evaluate the Inner Subquery</strong><br>The subquery finds <code>M.pid</code> where <code>C.cname = 'Mark'</code>:<br>1. From table <code>coach</code>, <code>cname = 'Mark'</code> gives <code>cid = 102</code>.<br>2. From table <code>team</code>, where <code>T.cid = 102</code>, we get <code>tid = 10</code>.<br>3. From table <code>members</code>, where <code>M.tid = 10</code>, we get <code>pid</code> values <code>1</code> and <code>3</code>.<br><br>So, the inner subquery returns the set <code>{1, 3}</code>.<br><br><strong>Step 2: Evaluate the Outer Query</strong><br>The outer query selects the minimum <code>age</code> from <code>player</code> where <code>pid</code> is in <code>{1, 3}</code>:<br>1. For <code>pid = 1</code>, <code>age = 31</code>.<br>2. For <code>pid = 3</code>, <code>age = 26</code>.<br><br>The minimum of <code>{31, 26}</code> is <code>26</code>.<br><br>Thus, the value returned by the query is <strong>26</strong>.",
